**Effective Date:** January 1, 2024

Schedule.Skin ("us", "we", or "our") operates the schedule.skin website and the related vanity URL Services (the "Service"). This page informs you of our policies regarding the collection, use, and disclosure of personal data when you use our Service.

### 1. Information Collection and Use
We collect several different types of information to provide and improve our Service to clinicians.
- **Personal Data:** While using our Service, we may ask you to provide us with certain personally identifiable information (e.g., Email, Clinic Name, Booking Links).
- **Patient Data:** Schedule.Skin does not store patient medical records or individual appointment data. Any information entered by your clients is handled directly by your primary booking provider.

### 2. Tracking & Cookies Data
We use cookies and similar tracking technologies to track activity on our Service and hold certain information. You can instruct your browser to refuse all cookies, though some portions of the Service may become inaccessible.

### 3. Use of Data
Schedule.Skin uses the collected data for various purposes:
- To provide and maintain the vanity URL service.
- To notify you about changes to our Service.
- To provide customer support and "White-Glove" setup.
- To monitor the technical usage of the Service.

### 4. Security of Data
The security of your data is important to us, but remember that no method of transmission over the Internet is 100% secure. We utilize commercially acceptable means to protect your Personal Data but cannot guarantee its absolute security.

### 5. Payment Processing
Payments are processed via secure third-party gateways. We do not store your credit card or bank account information on our servers.

### 6. Governing Law
This Privacy Policy and our privacy practices are governed by the laws of **the State of Delaware, United States**, without regard to its conflict of law principles. Any legal actions related to this policy shall be brought exclusively in the state or federal courts located in the State of Delaware.

### 7. Contact Us
If you have any questions about this Privacy Policy, please contact us through our [Contact Page](/contact).

